    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525-a10">

                <pb facs="0821" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg693"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9 in No.
                    312.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pueyo to Mr.
                            Vickers</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Local Administration of the Custom-House</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Matanzas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1884-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 14, 1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Under date of yesterday this office addressed to Mr. E. S. Henley the
                    following:</p>
                <p>“In the discharge of the American barkentine Ocean Pearl there resulted short ten
                    empty hogsheads, for which reason, in conformity with paragraph 13, article 121,
                    chapter 2 of the general ordinances of the bureau, you have incurred a fine of
                    $200 for each one of the packages which have not been discharged, which sum,
                    amounting to $2,000, should be paid into this office as soon as possible,
                    through your consignees.”</p>
                <p>All of which I communicate to you, acceding to what you requested in your
                    official letter of the 13th instant.</p>
                <p>May God guard you many years.</p>
                <closer><signed>RAFAEL PUEYO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
